{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1782087783941,"sessionID":"ses_1134b197affeltRDVI502UKukp","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_6062f896aaa543e098cabc02","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"{\n  \"name\": \"brazilian-soccer-mcp\",\n  \"version\": \"2.0.0\",\n  \"description\": \"MCP server providing a knowledge graph interface for Brazilian soccer data\",\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"main\": \"dist/index.js\",\n  \"bin\": {\n    \"brazilian-soccer-mcp\": \"dist/index.js\"\n  },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"build\": \"tsc -p tsconfig.json\",\n    \"clean\": \"rm -rf dist\",\n    \"start\": \"node dist/index.js\",\n    \"test\": \"node --test --test-reporter=spec dist/tests/*.test.js\",\n    \"typecheck\": \"tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json\",\n    \"lint\": \"eslint . --ext .ts || true\"\n  },\n  \"license\": \"MIT\",\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@modelcontextprotocol/sdk\": \"^1.0.0\",\n    \"csv-parse\": \"^5.6.0\",\n    \"zod\": \"^3.23.0\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@types/node\": \"^22.0.0\",\n    \"typescript\": \"^5.6.0\"\n  },\n  \"engines\": {\n    \"node\": \">=20\"\n  }\n}\n","filePath":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-1zdmpvud/retort-6eb2808ba107/package.json"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-1zdmpvud/retort-6eb2808ba107/package.json","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"package.json","time":{"start":1782087783934,"end":1782087783939}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now let me plan the implementation. I'll set up a TypeScript project with:\n- `package.json` with dependencies: `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk`, `csv-parse`, `zod`; dev deps for tests\n- `tsconfig.json`\n- Source files under `src/`:\n  - `types.ts` - shared types\n  - `normalize.ts` - team name normalization\n  - `loaders/` - CSV loaders for each file\n  - `queries/` - query handlers\n  - `server.ts` - MCP server with tool registrations\n  - `index.ts` - entrypoint\n- Tests under `tests/` using a BDD-style structure. The TASK says use BDD GWT structured tests. Since this is TypeScript, I'll use a simple test runner — maybe vitest. But the spec says \"BDD GWT structured\" — I can structure tests as Given/When/Then with vitest's describe/it.\n\nLet me keep dependencies minimal to avoid network issues. Use csv-parse for CSV. For testing, vitest. For MCP, use @modelcontextprotocol/sdk.\n\nLet me set up the project and write everything. Let me start with package.json.\n\nActually, to minimize external packages, I can implement CSV parsing manually but csv-parse is more reliable for edge cases (quoted fields with commas, etc.). Let me use csv-parse/sync.\n\nLet me create the project.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_eecb57e29001Sqa85Xs93UVU7T","sessionID":"ses_1134b197affeltRDVI502UKukp","messageID":"msg_eecb56fef001P9M1L7Nkk3Jz1c"}}
